# The pictures of sketch-on-face.md: a base, its top face picked, a
# sketch started on it, a rectangle drawn there and extruded into a
# column; then the base made thicker, and the column going up with it.
size tw 760 600
key r
move 200 200
down L 200 200
up L 200 200
move 380 330
down L 380 330
up L 380 330
key esc
key x shift
# The base's depth held at 10.
twmove 505 128
twdown L 505 128
twup L 505 128
twmove 510 128
twdown L 510 128
twup L 510 128
edit 10
move 290 265
down L 290 265
up L 290 265
view rotated
menu View|Zoom To Fit
shot sketch-on-face-1-face
menu Features|Sketch On Face
menu View|Zoom To Fit
menu View|Zoom Out
shot sketch-on-face-2-workplane
view default
key r
move 250 230
down L 250 230
up L 250 230
move 330 300
down L 330 300
up L 330 300
key esc
view rotated
menu View|Zoom To Fit
shot sketch-on-face-3-rectangle gw
key x shift
# The column's depth held at 30.
twmove 505 128
twdown L 505 128
twup L 505 128
twmove 510 128
twdown L 510 128
twup L 510 128
edit 30
view rotated
menu View|Zoom To Fit
shot sketch-on-face-4-column
twmove 30 13
twdown L 30 13
twup L 30 13
# The base made 25 thick from its own screen: the column goes up.
twmove 150 163
twdown L 150 163
twup L 150 163
twmove 510 128
twdown L 510 128
twup L 510 128
edit 25
view rotated
menu View|Zoom To Fit
shot sketch-on-face-5-thicker
